      "claim": "(+)-Bicuculline, a close phthalideisoquinoline analog sharing the lactone, methylenedioxy, and N-methyl motifs, penetrated rat brain in a dose-dependent manner measured by LC-MS/MS, supporting CNS access for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "α-Allocryptopine was detected in rat CSF after administration, demonstrating passage across the blood-brain barrier; its dimethoxy/methylenedioxy isoquinoline scaffold is directly relevant to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "Tetrahydroberberine was detected in rat CSF, indicating effective BBB penetration; this tetrahydroprotoberberine shares the N-methyl, dimethoxy, and methylenedioxy features of the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "Schisandrin B showed a relatively high brain/plasma equilibration rate with logPSFu,brain of -3.2 and was classified as permeable, supporting that polycyclic dimethoxy/methylenedioxy natural products of this class can access the brain.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "Isocorydine was detected in rat brain within 10 minutes of administration, showing rapid BBB crossing; its N-methyl dimethoxy/methylenedioxy aporphine-like scaffold is analogous to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "Nuciferine reached brain concentrations nearly equal to plasma in rats, demonstrating meaningful CNS access for an N-methyl dimethoxy isoquinoline alkaloid closely related to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "Corydaline was detected in rat CSF and showed brain levels close to other tissues, confirming effective BBB penetration for a tetrahydroprotoberberine with the same dimethoxy/methylenedioxy substitution pattern.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "Boldine crossed the blood-brain barrier with high brain concentrations after oral administration, providing additional support that N-methylated dimethoxy isoquinoline alkaloids achieve meaningful CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is noscapine, a phthalideisoquinoline alkaloid. Multiple structurally related alkaloids—bicuculline, allocryptopine, tetrahydroberberine, corydaline, isocorydine, nuciferine, boldine, and schisandrin B—show direct brain or CSF penetration in rats/mice. These transferable in vivo data, together with favorable passive BBB properties, support a pass for meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct noscapine-specific brain/CSF pharmacokinetic record was provided, though the analog evidence is strong.",
    "Quantitative unbound brain-to-plasma ratios or CSF-to-plasma ratios are not available for the query itself.",
    "No direct P-gp or BCRP efflux assay data are available for noscapine, but the high neutral fraction and analog CNS penetration reduce this concern."
